{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded","id":1427669,"title":"How important are auspicious signs among the Dragon Blooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-07T19:36:53-08:00","id":1427669,"title":"How important are auspicious signs among the Dragon Blooded?","content":"I'm prepping to run a Dragon-Blooded campaign, and my players and I took a liking to the idea of them being part of a Cadet house that we are planning out for the game. The players are all siblings born at the same time. Basically a triplet group that all exalted. I worked up that their Mother, the house Matriarch, completed the pilgrimage of The Caul and the following pregnancy resulted in these children. I am already aware that the likelihood of all three exalting is next to impossible, but when It's the game we all want to play it doesn't matter how unlikely something is. I'm looking for second opinions on how significant this or other auspicious occurrences might reflect on the Dragon-Blooded as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T20:40:35-08:00","id":1427673,"title":"","content":"To put it mildly? It's next to impossible for more than one twin to become Exalted, and triplets magnifies that impossibility by a factor of three. If all three do in fact exalt, people aren't going to immediately assume that it's a sign from the dragons or something. They're going to be wondering &quot;...Did the mother just <i>adopt</i> two other children that just so happened to exalt?&quot; because that will be a more believable premise than what you've stated. There's also a chance they could think that something demonic is afoot, but considering that the Immaculate Order says that being Exalted as a Dragon-Blooded is the only &quot;true&quot; way to be Exalted, as it's a sign of spiritual purity, this is quite unlikely, otherwise it would taint the idea of Terrestrial superiority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T03:12:31-08:00","id":1427689,"title":"","content":"If you're one of three triplets that all exalted, you're definitely gonna be <i>known </i>as &quot;the triplets who all managed to exalt&quot;. Some more superstitions individuals might take it as a portent or a sign you're destined for great things, but I think most would just be &quot;wow, crazy. what are the odds?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T04:03:02-08:00","id":1427693,"title":"","content":"Like in real life, the level of superstition varies from culture to culture and person to person.<br /> <br /> As a Cadet House, and thus outside of the Dynasty proper but linked strongly to the Realm, I suspect most will view this with suspicion. But as a Caul pilgrimage is already in play, I don't think many people will view it as some great conspiracy. You could absolutely have a character with any reaction you'd care to name -- there's a real gambit of appropriate responses from complete indifference to outright hostility.<br /> <br /> They will definitely be known as &quot;the triplets who all Exalted&quot;. My game has a pair of twins who both Exalted who get referred to as &quot;the twins&quot; with drama around the youngest kid constantly looking to prove he's more than his sister's leftovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-09-2020, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T13:58:13-08:00","id":1427749,"title":"","content":"In regards to how people react, given that there seem to be a lot of different possibilities, I think a good question is &quot;Which reactions would create interesting conflict, that the players are invested in&quot;?<br /> <br /> That's why I definitely think there should be negative reaction, with people arguing everything from the mundane &quot;she slept with whichever man with very good breeding or who also went on a Caul pilgrimage it would be most politically inconvenient to be the father&quot; to the absurd &quot;she consorted with Anathema to steal Exaltations that rightfully should have went to spiritually pure Dynasts and instead foisted them on her children, who weren't ready for them, as demonstrated by [whatever trouble they've gotten themselves into]&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is not necessarily because they find the triple Exaltation unbelievable, but because other people believe that it is an auspicious sign, meaning that the PCs would be good candidates for positions of responsibility, or at least a sign of good breeding, meaning that the PCs would be good candidates for a marriage above their station, and people competing for the same positions would have reason to come up with dark rumors and other counterarguments.<br /> <br /> An interesting question is what the PC's mother should think. I feel like &quot;their mother thinks they would be good candidates for an advantageous marriage, but not necessarily for a dangerous mission&quot; is a good setup for classic stories about avoiding parental pressure for a political marriage and sneaking off to go on dangerous adventures, while &quot;their mother thinks that their auspicious birth implies they would be well-suited to, e.g., conquer new territory for the Realm&quot; is good if the players prefer to skip that stuff and go straight to the dangerous adventure. One can adjust as appropriate for your particular game, I hope.<br /> <br /> Another think to think about is if anything could make this event less unlikely, and whether it would be fun to have any of that in the backstory. I don't know exactly what the mechanics of Caul pilgrimages are supposed to be, but surely if the father also went on a Caul pilgrimage (most likely together...), and they conceived the child on the Caul, it couldn't hurt the chances of something like this happening. A stranger idea is that the father is secretly a Lunar who went on the Caul pilgrimage, and owing to the Caul's origin in love between Luna and Gaia, that combination had a dramatic effect on the children. That one seems like it would be fun to come up at some point in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:20:17-08:00","id":1427776,"title":"","content":"The effect of a successful pilgrimage is \u201cYour next child will exalt, guaranteed.\u201d That assumes a single birth though, and it\u2019s entirely possible that there could be no recorded instance of Caul-blessed twins for anyone to know what happens then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:40:57-08:00","id":1427781,"title":"","content":"I think multiple children Exalting on its own doesn't necessarily qualify as something auspicious, but if it coincides with some noteworthy event or phenomenon then I could see Dynasts regarding them as tied together. The birth of several of the children of the Scarlet Empress is accompanied by things like meteor showers or earthquakes that are regarded as having been portentous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T10:06:38-08:00","id":1427876,"title":"","content":"I can also see that (ST and player interest permitting) that Dragonblood already invested in reclaiming the Caul would latch on to the triplets and their parents as a rallying point -- not only did their mother's next birth Exalt, but she had triplets, all of whom exalted. It's less important that it's true (versus 'oh, she adopted two infants to cover for their actual births and just says they are triplets') than that it is useful. Though some may believe it is true.<br /> <br /> It also means that factions who see the Caul as a distraction might be more inclined to downplay the birth/exaltation.<br /> <br /> (My inner ST really likes the idea of the father being a Lunar, simply because it would be a result that would cause the most plot hooks if revealed. It would assume a Caul or Lunars-focused game, though. If it's not, then one might just go with 'few enough people complete the pilgrimage that this may be the first recorded birth of multiples after the pilgrimage, so maybe this is normal?')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24133-stareyes","name":"Stareyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T11:17:18-08:00","id":1427881,"title":"","content":"I cannot imagine any circumstances in which somebody pretends to have extra children on top of their actual pregnancy. It just seems like an unnecessary added expense when there are surely childless members of the House that can take them in.<br /> <br /> Heck, considering expenses, triplets or higher actually seems more like a circumstance where some of them would be adopted out to other households. Sure you're rolling the dice on keeping the one that inherited the Essence, but that might be a price worth paying to relieve the burdens.<br /> <br /> Gets the added bonus of the unlikely triple Exaltation getting them shipped as a unit when they actually haven't grown up together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T12:16:38-08:00","id":1427891,"title":"","content":"You can't imagine why the Matriarch of a Cadet House might want to appear more fertile than she is? Why she might want an excuse to apportion more of her family's resources to her own purse? Why she might want to increase the chances of her kids Exalting (not so much if she's done a Caul pilgrimage)? Why she might want to &quot;wear the pillow&quot; if one of her marriagable female scions has got into trouble and jepodized their engagement to a Dynast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T16:26:59-08:00","id":1427917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427891#post1427891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't imagine why the Matriarch of a Cadet House might want to appear more fertile than she is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can set aside the question of whether or not multiple births has much to do with fertility (I don't know offhand myself) because it doesn't really matter, I can assume Dynasts would assume so in ignorance. But I still see flaws in this idea.<br /> <br /> Who is this Exalt trying to entice with such an image? If she's already married, it's a bit well past that point, and if she's not then I think leading with having gotten three natural children unlikely to Exalt but still have to be raised with the usual expenses for the price of one is not very compelling to the mothers of prospective husbands.<br /> <br /> Is appearing very fertile really a thing that the Dragon Blooded want? You're in a society that simultaneously values having only one child every decade or two and recreational sex, it seems to me that you don't generally want it to seem like birth control needs to work too hard to keep plans and finances from being scuppered.<br /> <br /> It's another matter to compensate for being outright infertile (was this proposing a scenario in which one embellishes on their existing pregnancy?), but going for the image of triplets seems overkill to the point of counterproductive, because you're making the image of &quot;pregnancy comes with two leftover children as a matter of course&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why she might want an excuse to apportion more of her family's resources to her own purse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, resources you claim for having children are supposed to then be spent on those children. I can only imagine the faux pas inherent to embezzling your kid's education fund. I have to assume there are much more straightforward ways to get that money that don't come with the bad press.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why she might want to increase the chances of her kids Exalting (not so much if she's done a Caul pilgrimage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one you're going to have to explain a bit more to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why she might want to &quot;wear the pillow&quot; if one of her marriagable female scions has got into trouble and jepodized their engagement to a Dynast?</div> </div> </div> </div>That just leads back to the question of if this family does not have any other members that are currently not pregnant.<br /> <br /> That to me is the only one that makes sense, if the usual circumstances for pretend pregnancy to legitimise a child are in play but literally everybody is pregnant at the time.<br /> <br /> Mind, if you want to pass them off as twins or triplets then it still only works with a person who fell pregnant at the same time as the accident was conceived, unless one wants to go through a game of keeping the first born baby hidden until things line up to pass them off as sequential.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T22:21:10-08:00","id":1427943,"title":"","content":"Personally i hated the &quot;dragon bloods are wary to use up their spiritual puissance. People like to fuck, its kind of what we're known for. In this setting people fuck EVERYTHING. From animals, to spirits, to ghosts, to trees. Also while its not probable it is possible and this is exalted. Don't forget the rule of cool (or whatever the story teller lets you get away with) trumps all. If your momma had three kids that all exalt together? Then awesome. Especially since lookshy doesn't really seem to care about managing bloodlines as much and the other dragonblooded factions tend to have the view of &quot;you make it you take care of it... or don't?&quot; Maybe mamma found a super cool tea that is ultra rare and gifts exalted babies, maybe mamma did a caul pilgrimage three times 100 years ago when the realm owned all the settlements. Maybe she was touched by a minor elemental dragon. Do what you want with your story. All of canon or setting books are a loose guideline. I personally prefer the empress' disappearance being more in line with mnemon being overly ambitious as opposed to mating with a demon and giving up her already hegemonic status over creation to become a demons play thing. You do you friend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8897-joshopotamus","name":"joshopotamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T23:13:29-08:00","id":1427944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427917#post1427917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one you're going to have to explain a bit more to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best possible bloodlines only have an 80% chance of Exalting. A cadet house is unlikely to have such a bloodline.<br /> <br /> Having three kids gives you three rolls of the dice.<br /> <br /> Adopting two extra kids who aren't yours gives you three full sets of progenative Essence.<br /> <br /> (It's a Prince Caspian kinda deal: better the niece you've raised rule than a stranger.)<br /> <br /> And if two fail to Exalted... well that's not because you are a thin-blooded threshold whelp: it's because they are leftover children. Yours is a proud and strong bloodline and any Dragon-Blooded would be fortunate to marry your children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T03:54:55-08:00","id":1427954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427944#post1427944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having three kids gives you three rolls of the dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives you one good roll and two incredibly bad ones but where the social expectation remains to bring them all up as though success is an absolute certainty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adopting two extra kids who aren't yours gives you three full sets of progenative Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is giving up their full-blooded children to a cadet House? And why are they still going through the charade of acting like it's a natural pregnancy, invariably reserved for collecting children from out of wedlock (thus typically half thin-blooded)?<br /> <br /> If they all somehow have full progenitive Essence then pretending they're triplets is a terrible idea, because it'll make society assume two of them have worse bloodlines than they do and make marriage negotiations harder than necessary. They should just be openly adopted, as is a thing in the Dynasty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if two fail to Exalted... well that's not because you are a thin-blooded threshold whelp: it's because they are leftover children. Yours is a proud and strong bloodline and any Dragon-Blooded would be fortunate to marry your children.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're triplets than they're leftover children regardless and Exalting at all is beating the odds. The way the book describes it, leftover Essence is no better from strong bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I feel as though the culture presented to us is one that will more likely laugh off as an uneducated tube the cadet House member that tries to claim three Exalted children as displaying a particularly puissant bloodline. Heck, bring that to any family with twins where only the one Exalted and I can see a claim like that being a grave insult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T05:38:18-08:00","id":1427961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427954#post1427954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we've segwayed here.<br /> <br /> This thread is about a matriarch whose triplets all Exalted.<br /> <br /> WFHW suggests this is very unlikely.<br /> <br /> When unexpected things happen, humans invent conspiracy theories. I'm not going to list real life conspiracy theories but I assure you that people believe plenty of things that aren't logical. I think that folks inventing conspiracy theories when a member of an outgroup does something unlikely but desirable is probable.<br /> <br /> (Likewise, Stareyes suggested that one might claim that three Exalts are triplets specifically to attest to the importance of the Caul as a political manuerver -- which is what started this tangent.)<br /> <br /> As to why someone of personal power might adopt a child of great potential or why a parent might give their child up for adoption (outside of the wild, baseless accusations of one's enemies used to discredit you -- which is what we're talking about here), I feel like these are fertile topics for their own threads. I will be bowing out of this tangent here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-10-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T07:40:20-08:00","id":1427972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427917#post1427917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just leads back to the question of if this family does not have any other members that are currently not pregnant.<br /> <br /> That to me is the only one that makes sense, if the usual circumstances for pretend pregnancy to legitimise a child are in play but literally everybody is pregnant at the time.<br /> <br /> Mind, if you want to pass them off as twins or triplets then it still only works with a person who fell pregnant at the same time as the accident was conceived, unless one wants to go through a game of keeping the first born baby hidden until things line up to pass them off as sequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would focus on this conspiracy theory, especially if you don't like the other ones, because it is both particularly plausible (as you note) and particularly interesting / scandalous.<br /> <br /> I don't think it literally requires everyone to be pregnant, The PCs just need to have, like, an older sister and a cousin who can be accused of hiding pregnancies. They can still have another sister, a niece or two, and another cousin who aren't. Would this mean that the PC's house has been growing in numbers recently, making it hard for them to maintain quite the same standard of luxury that they were used to, and leading to potential conflict within the family? Probably! Will the PCs, when they Exalt, be expected to find new sources of wealth to fix this? Seems like a good idea to me.<br /> <br /> The theory of multiple people in the same house having unwanted pregnancies at the same time is unlikely. But the only thing that matters, to people spreading the conspiracy theory, is that it seems more likely, to them, than triplets Exalting. Presumably the way Caul pilgrimages work with multiple pregnancies is unknown and, these people theorize, it only applies to whichever child leaves the womb first, which would leave the second and third incredibly unlikely to Exalt. Thus, even very unlikely, but possible, conspiracy explanations would be preferred.<br /> <br /> Plus, maybe the women got pregnant at the same time because of their involvement in a particularly debauched party organized by House Cynis. That sort of lurid tale would ensure the rumors spread, even if there wasn't much evidence behind it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T07:43:08-08:00","id":1427973,"title":"","content":"By all means though I do love this discussion assuming it does not get heated enough to engender hard feelings. I was looking for other opinions on how the circumstance my players wanted might affect them both positively and negatively and this debate seems like something that might circle this discussion among dynasts not related to the matter but speculating none the less. I have always found it invaluable to get opinions outside my own when determining how a general mass might react to a situation to avoid everyone seeming to be of one mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T09:36:45-08:00","id":1427995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427972#post1427972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would focus on this conspiracy theory, especially if you don't like the other ones, because it is both particularly plausible (as you note) and particularly interesting / scandalous.<br /> <br /> I don't think it literally requires everyone to be pregnant, The PCs just need to have, like, an older sister and a cousin who can be accused of hiding pregnancies. They can still have another sister, a niece or two, and another cousin who aren't. Would this mean that the PC's house has been growing in numbers recently, making it hard for them to maintain quite the same standard of luxury that they were used to, and leading to potential conflict within the family? Probably! Will the PCs, when they Exalt, be expected to find new sources of wealth to fix this? Seems like a good idea to me.<br /> <br /> The theory of multiple people in the same house having unwanted pregnancies at the same time is unlikely. But the only thing that matters, to people spreading the conspiracy theory, is that it seems more likely, to them, than triplets Exalting. Presumably the way Caul pilgrimages work with multiple pregnancies is unknown and, these people theorize, it only applies to whichever child leaves the womb first, which would leave the second and third incredibly unlikely to Exalt. Thus, even very unlikely, but possible, conspiracy explanations would be preferred.<br /> <br /> Plus, maybe the women got pregnant at the same time because of their involvement in a particularly debauched party organized by House Cynis. That sort of lurid tale would ensure the rumors spread, even if there wasn't much evidence behind it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Women in the Scarlet Dynasty not wanting their children is a bit odd, but going through secrecy seems unnecessary when they're already in your House. Again, adoption does happen, generally in the form of transferring kids around the House. <br /> <br /> Like sure, it makes sense that sometimes Dynasts become pregnant at a time unsuited to them (and times they're deemed just awful parents by the matriarch), but you can just make arrangements with, like, your gay brother and his younger husband to bring up the kid.<br /> <br /> Pretend pregnancies are where you want legal claim to a kid being carried by somebody outside of the House, because of the matrilineality; a contingency for the indiscretions of men. It's totally unnecessary if you're already a member of the House you want the kid to stay in.<br /> <br /> I have to imagine a Dynast woman conspiring to give her child to a different Great House is far more stigmatized than any of this. <br /> <br /> Although I suppose I'm open to somebody devising a compelling enough very individual situation for why they're all doing this, although I would think it needs to involve somebody being coerced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T09:53:46-08:00","id":1427998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427995#post1427995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Women in the Scarlet Dynasty not wanting their children is a bit odd, but going through secrecy seems unnecessary when they're already in your House. Again, adoption does happen, generally in the form of transferring kids around the House.<br /> <br /> Like sure, it makes sense that sometimes Dynasts become pregnant at a time unsuited to them (and times they're deemed just awful parents by the matriarch), but you can just make arrangements with, like, your gay brother and his younger husband to bring up the kid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the theory is that they had important marriages agreed to which haven't yet occurred or been consummated. I know a woman's children are always legitimate, but I think the spouse and his house would be at least a bit annoyed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pretend pregnancies are where you want legal claim to a kid being carried by somebody outside of the House, because of the matrilineality; a contingency for the indiscretions of men. It's totally unnecessary if you're already a member of the House you want the kid to stay in. </div> </div> </div>So maybe it would be better for the theory to be that male members of the House had children with lesser-status women, wanted to keep them and to keep them in the house, but didn't want to face judgment for risking the progenitive essence they were supposed to spend on their wives, and asked their Matriarch to secretly pay the mothers to give up their children (or coerce them in other ways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T14:11:51-08:00","id":1428804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1427954#post1427954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the culture presented to us is one that will more likely laugh off as an uneducated tube the cadet House member that tries to claim three Exalted children as displaying a particularly puissant bloodline. Heck, bring that to any family with twins where only the one Exalted and I can see a claim like that being a grave insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is relevant to my thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the key difference between an auspicious sign and foolish superstition is power and privilege. A cadet house matriarch is in an interesting place for that because she's potentially very powerful in her own limited sphere but on the Blessed Isle they are likely to be reminded of their limitations. Back when the Scarlet Empress was around there might have been an additional incentive to have someone like this assassinated before they started to look like someone the Empress might want to adopt and groom as a future Great House leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T04:06:58-08:00","id":1428841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1427669-how-important-are-auspicious-signs-among-the-dragon-blooded?p=1428804#post1428804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, the key difference between an auspicious sign and foolish superstition is power and privilege.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit like ancient Rome. They accused druids of human sacrifice, marking them as despicable and uncivilised. Totally different from their practice of hanging captured enemy leaders in front of the temple of Jupiter at the end of triumphs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}